::GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.1<br><br>Question:<br>Which rule translates a point 4 units right and 3 units down? {
= (x, y) &rarr; (x + 4, y - 3)#Correct. (x, y) &rarr; (x + 4, y - 3) matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (x - 4, y + 3)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (x - 4, y + 3). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (-x, y)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (-x, y). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ (x, y) &rarr; (y, x)#This choice reflects a misconception: (x, y) &rarr; (y, x). Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q02::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.2<br><br>Question:<br>Which transformation preserves distance? {
~ Dilation with scale factor 2#This choice reflects a misconception: Dilation with scale factor 2. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ Vertical stretch#This choice reflects a misconception: Vertical stretch. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
= Reflection#Correct. Reflection matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ Horizontal compression#This choice reflects a misconception: Horizontal compression. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q03::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.4<br><br>Question:<br>A figure maps onto itself after a 180 degree turn. What symmetry is shown? {
~ Reflection symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception: Reflection symmetry. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
= Rotation symmetry#Correct. Rotation symmetry matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ Translation symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception: Translation symmetry. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ No symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception: No symmetry. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q04::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.6<br><br>Question:<br>A rigid motion maps one figure exactly onto another. What conclusion is supported? {
= The figures are congruent#Correct. The figures are congruent matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ The figures are different sizes#This choice reflects a misconception: The figures are different sizes. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ Only one angle matches#This choice reflects a misconception: Only one angle matches. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ The figures are unrelated#This choice reflects a misconception: The figures are unrelated. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L08_GP_Q05::
